.TH "NOTMUCH-NEW" "1" "Apr 17, 2026" "0.40" "notmuch"
.SH "نام (NAME)"
notmuch-new \- incorporate new mail into the notmuch database
.SH "خلاصه دستور (SYNOPSIS)"
.sp
\fBnotmuch\fP \fBnew\fP [options]
.SH "توضیحات (DESCRIPTION)"
.sp
Find and import any new messages to the database.
.sp
The \fBnew\fP command scans all sub\-directories of the database,
performing full\-text indexing on new messages that are found. Each new
message will automatically be tagged with both the \fBinbox\fP and
\fBunread\fP tags.
.sp
You should run \fBnotmuch new\fP once after first running
notmuch \%<#\:notmuch-setup-1> to create the initial database. The first run
may take a long time if you have a significant amount of mail (several
hundred thousand messages or more). Subsequently, you should run
\fBnotmuch new\fP whenever new mail is delivered and you wish to
incorporate it into the database.  These subsequent runs will be much
quicker than the initial run.
.sp
Invoking \fBnotmuch\fP with no command argument will run \fBnew\fP if
notmuch \%<#\:notmuch-setup-1> has previously been completed, but \fBnotmuch
new\fP has not previously been run.
.sp
\fBnotmuch new\fP updates tags according to maildir flag changes if the
\fBmaildir.synchronize_flags\fP configuration option is enabled. See
notmuch\-config \%<#\:notmuch-config-1> for details.
.sp
The \fBnew\fP command supports hooks. See notmuch\-hooks \%<#\:notmuch-hooks-5> for more
details on hooks.
.sp
Supported options for \fBnew\fP include
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \-\-no\-hooks
Prevents hooks from being run.
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \-\-quiet
Do not print progress or results.
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \-\-verbose
Print file names being processed. Ignored when combined with
\fB\-\-quiet\fP\&.
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \-\-decrypt=(true|nostash|auto|false)
If \fBtrue\fP, when encountering an encrypted message, try to
decrypt it while indexing, and stash any discovered session keys.
If \fBauto\fP, try to use any session key already known to belong to
this message, but do not attempt to use the user\(aqs secret keys.
If decryption is successful, index the cleartext of the message.
.sp
Be aware that the index is likely sufficient (and the session key
is certainly sufficient) to reconstruct the cleartext of the
message itself, so please ensure that the notmuch message index is
adequately protected.  DO NOT USE \fB\-\-decrypt=true\fP or
\fB\-\-decrypt=nostash\fP without considering the security of your
index.
.sp
See also \fBindex.decrypt\fP in notmuch\-config \%<#\:notmuch-config-1>\&.
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \-\-full\-scan
By default notmuch\-new uses directory modification times (mtimes)
to optimize the scanning of directories for new mail. This option turns
that optimization off.
.UNINDENT
.SH "پیکربندی (CONFIGURATION)"
.sp
Indexing is influenced by the configuration options
index.decrypt \%<#\:nmconfig-index\:.decrypt>, index.header.<prefix> \%<#\:nmconfig-index\:.header\:.-prefix>
and new.ignore \%<#\:nmconfig-new\:.ignore>\&.  Tagging
is controlled by new.tags \%<#\:nmconfig-new\:.tags> and
maildir.synchronize_flags \%<#\:nmconfig-maildir\:.synchronize_flags>\&.  See
notmuch\-config \%<#\:notmuch-config-1> for details.
.SH "وضعیت خروج (EXIT STATUS)"
.sp
This command supports the following special exit status code
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \fB75 (EX_TEMPFAIL)\fP
A temporary failure occurred; the user is invited to retry.
.UNINDENT
.SH "همچنین ببینید (SEE ALSO)"
.sp
notmuch \%<#\:notmuch-1>,
notmuch\-config \%<#\:notmuch-config-1>,
notmuch\-count \%<#\:notmuch-count-1>,
notmuch\-dump \%<#\:notmuch-dump-1>,
notmuch\-hooks \%<#\:notmuch-hooks-5>,
notmuch\-insert \%<#\:notmuch-insert-1>,
notmuch\-reply \%<#\:notmuch-reply-1>,
notmuch\-restore \%<#\:notmuch-restore-1>,
notmuch\-search \%<#\:notmuch-search-1>,
notmuch\-search\-terms \%<#\:notmuch-search-terms-7>,
notmuch\-show \%<#\:notmuch-show-1>,
notmuch\-tag \%<#\:notmuch-tag-1>
.SH "نویسنده (AUTHOR)"
Carl Worth and many others
